Report & Public Petitions
10. PUBLIC HEARING regarding a request for the vacation of a portion of
the existing 80-ft of the public right-of-way of Rd 103 also known as
BCH CR 10 and McLees Rd, as identified on exhibit A.
25 - 031
Viewer's Report, Road 103, RP# 512
Attachments:
Molly Bennett, Public Works, and Scott Larson, appointed viewer, reported to the
board that they recommend granting the vacation.
Acting Chairman Thompson opened the hearing for PUBLIC COMMENT. Bonnie
Reider, applicant, spoke in support of the vacation for security reasons. Hearing no
further PUBLIC COMMENT, Acting Chairman Thompson closed the hearing.
Acting Chairman Thompson said he received an email from Charlie Farthing,
resident, in favor of the vacation.
A motion was made by Commissioner Heath, seconded by Commissioner
Zwonitzer, that this agenda item be approved. The motion carried by the
following vote:
Thompson, Heath, Hollingshead, Zwonitzer
Aye:
Malm
Excused:
